* Generic (non-PDK) NMOS corner models standing in for sky130's own tt/ss/ff
* process split -- same "runs anywhere ngspice runs" precedent as
* examples/kb/rc-relaxation-oscillator/corners.lib. VTO/KP/LAMBDA move
* together the way a real sky130 corner split would move an NMOS's drive
* strength and output resistance. Replace with a real sky130 model library
* (models.pdk / models.lib pointing at $PDK_ROOT) once this task is re-run
* against real devices -- see README.md "Known limitation" note.
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.55 KP=100u LAMBDA=0.04)

.lib tt
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.50 KP=120u LAMBDA=0.05)
.endl tt

.lib ss
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.60 KP=95u LAMBDA=0.04)
.endl ss

.lib ff
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.40 KP=145u LAMBDA=0.06)
.endl ff
